data declared_method_roster_note: String = "The single declared authority for METHOD NAMES the substrate provides (§3). Each entry references its MethodDeclaration row rather than restating the string, so the name lives in exactly one place and a new method is one row plus one reference. Consumer: v1.compiler.infer method-existence wall (method_existence_wall_note) — a method name absent from this roster AND not found on a fully-resolved receiver is provably not dispatchable, so it refuses at compile time instead of reaching InterpError::Unimplemented. This roster is NOT yet reconciled against the interpreter native dispatch arms or the per-target emit handlers; that reconciliation is the primitive-realization-single-authority lane, and until it lands the roster is the CONSERVATIVE side of the fork (a name here is admitted without proving the receiver actually offers it). Measured evidence that the fork is real: count is declared here AND dispatched natively by the interpreter (the length/count/size arm) but is ABSENT from free_monoid_scalar_templates, so String.count() resolves at runtime while the algebra profile denies it."
